# ACCESS Backend Login Implementation Plan

## 1. Goal

Implement the simplest backend login system for ACCESS.

The login system should allow seeded internal users to authenticate using:

```txt
email + password
```

After successful login, backend returns:

```txt
JWT token + user profile
```

This login system is only for internal ACCESS users:

```txt
agent
manager
admin
```

No public registration is needed in this phase.

---

## 2. Auth Scope

Build only these endpoints:

```txt
POST /api/v1/auth/login
GET  /api/v1/auth/me
```

Do not build yet:

```txt
register
refresh token
forgot password
email verification
OAuth
cookie session
logout blacklist
multi-device session tracking
```

---

## 3. Tech Stack

```txt
Runtime: Bun
Framework: Elysia
Language: TypeScript
Database: PostgreSQL
ORM: Drizzle ORM
Auth: Bearer JWT
Password Hashing: bcrypt or Bun.password
```

Recommended for simplicity:

```txt
JWT: @elysiajs/jwt
Password Hashing: bcrypt
```

Install packages:

```bash
bun add @elysiajs/jwt bcrypt
bun add -d @types/bcrypt
```

---

## 4. Expected Login Flow

```txt
Client sends email + password
↓
Backend validates request body
↓
Backend finds user by email
↓
Backend checks user exists
↓
Backend checks user is active
↓
Backend compares password with password_hash
↓
Backend generates JWT
↓
Backend returns token and safe user profile
```

---

## 5. Expected Auth Header

Protected endpoints should receive token from:

```txt
Authorization: Bearer <token>
```

Example:

```txt
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI...
```

---

## 6. Environment Variables

Update `.env`:

```env
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/access_db
JWT_SECRET=access_dev_secret_change_later
JWT_EXPIRES_IN=7d
```

Important:

```txt
JWT_SECRET must not be hardcoded.
Use a stronger secret for production.
```

